            <ArticleTitle>Acute coronary syndromes: identification and patient care.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>289-92</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Acute coronary syndromes comprise acute ST-elevation myocardial infarction, non-ST-elevation myocardial infarction and unstable angina. These three conditions share a very similar pathology, although treatments differ. This paper examines the pathophysiology, identification, classification and management of these conditions.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
